From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] retain mission monitor until asynchronous STOP completes

0027 delivered 15 real AWDL frames to userspace with STA still associated,
but monitor deletion issued DELETE while STOP response was pending. Keep
the existing WMA reference until the normal STOP/timeout callback; send DOWN
then perform existing DP detach and reference release. No scheduler wait,
assert suppression, firmware change or TX enable. Only default-off gated
mission monitor in UP state uses this ordering. SME marks it logically deleted
before WMA detach, so the STOP dispatcher uses the existing no-state reference
API only as a gated monitor fallback; the retained WMA reference keeps it alive.
Runtime validation required.

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/inc/wma.h b/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/inc/wma.h
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/inc/wma.h
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/inc/wma.h
@@ -747,6 +747,8 @@
 	struct wma_invalid_peer_params invalid_peers[INVALID_PEER_MAX_NUM];
 	uint8_t invalid_peer_idx;
 	uint16_t bss_max_idle_period;
+	/* Gated mission monitor retains its WMA reference until STOP reply. */
+	bool marionette_monitor_detach_pending;
 };
 
